CHECK:AVOID_EXTERNS: extern prototypes should be avoided in .h files
#229: FILE: include/linux/user_namespace.h:139:
+extern struct user_namespace *get_user_ns_by_fd(int fd);

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'usize < CLONE_ARGS_SIZE_VER3'
#300: FILE: kernel/fork.c:2633:
+	if ((args.flags & CLONE_OWNER_NS) &&
+	    (usize < CLONE_ARGS_SIZE_VER3))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

